# Bank $A5's scripted figures (kind $08) through the scenes no play
# reaches, on the first level with the guard's record ($092B) in state 0
# ($4D, so GuardWait leaves its code word alone) and each cue poked once
# the figure waits on it.
# A. PlayerSceneDropIn ($A5:ED0F, way 4), resumed by its code word with
# its y at $0180 and gravity $38 ($20, 0 in its record) so it falls first; 128 frames, placed at spot $24, its
# leap, 48 frames, then waiting on the cues: the hurt count ($141B) set
# for 5 frames (its hurt pose), cue $BD set (its leap and fall), the
# player's $07 at $0D for a frame, cue $BE bit 7, and it runs and walks
# off.
load build/aladdin/states/level1.state
wait 10
poke 000978 00
poke 00093A 80,01
poke 00094B 38
poke 00092E 0F,ED
wait 300
poke 00141B 01
wait 5
poke 00141B 00
wait 5
poke 0000BD 01
wait 200
poke 0008E2 0D
wait 1
poke 0008E2 00
wait 80
poke 0000BE 80
wait 250
# B. PlayerSceneWalkOff ($A5:EE29, way 5) started with the copier RAM on:
# GuardStart's count ($1475) less 1 then differs from the cartridge RAM's
# byte, so it goes on at EscortStaySpot18 ($A5:EE36).
load build/aladdin/states/level1.state
cartram on
wait 10
poke 00092B 0C
poke 000932 05
wait 10
# C. PlayerSceneWalkOff resumed by its code word with its y at $0180 and
# gravity $38: it
# falls ($A5:EE3F), lands and walks; its x then set to $0F60, near its
# mark ($0F68): its poses, the run (it is past the player at once), 128
# frames facing left, cue $BD, and it walks on.
load build/aladdin/states/level1.state
cartram off
wait 10
poke 000978 00
poke 00093A 80,01
poke 00094B 38
poke 00092E 29,EE
wait 40
poke 000937 60,0F
wait 300
poke 0000BD 01
wait 40
